{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "name": "Titanium.UI.SearchBar",
  "kind": "view",
  "extends": "Titanium.UI.View",
  "inheritanceChain": [
    "Titanium.UI.View",
    "Titanium.Proxy"
  ],
  "platforms": [
    "android",
    "iphone",
    "ipad",
    "macos"
  ],
  "since": "0.8",
  "summary": "A specialized text field for entering search text.",
  "description": "| Android | iOS |\n| ------- | --- |\n| ![Android](./searchbar_android.png) | ![iOS](./searchbar_ios.png) |\n\nSearch bars are most commonly used for filtering the rows in a [TableView](api:Titanium.UI.TableView) and\n[ListView](api:Titanium.UI.ListView). You can add a search bar to a table view via its\n[search](api:Titanium.UI.TableView#search) property. You can add a search bar to a list view via its\n[searchBar](api:Titanium.UI.SearchBar) property.\n\nA search bar can also be used on its own.\n\nUse the [Titanium.UI.createSearchBar](api:Titanium.UI#createSearchBar) method or Alloy **`<SearchBar>`** element to create a search bar.\n\n#### Android Notes\n\nOn Android, the search bar's `[x]` clear button is used as a cancel button if\n[iconifiedByDefault](api:Titanium.UI.SearchBar#iconifiedByDefault) is set `true`,\ncausing it to collapse back into an icon. Otherwise, it will only clear the text\nand you'll receive a [change](api:Titanium.UI.SearchBar#change) event instead of a\n[cancel](api:Titanium.UI.SearchBar#cancel) event like iOS.\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Simple Search Bar",
      "code": "``` js\nvar search = Titanium.UI.createSearchBar({\n  barColor:'#000',\n  showCancel:true,\n  height:43,\n  top:0,\n});\n```\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Alloy XML Markup",
      "code": "Previous example as an Alloy view.\n\n``` xml\n<Alloy>\n    <SearchBar id=\"search\" barColor=\"#000\" showCancel=\"true\" height=\"43\" top=\"0\" />\n</Alloy>\n```\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Search Bar with TableView",
      "code": "``` js\nvar search = Ti.UI.createSearchBar({\n    showCancel: true\n});\nvar tableview = Ti.UI.createTableView({\n    search: search\n});\n```\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Alloy XML Markup",
      "code": "Previous example as an Alloy view.\n\n``` xml\n<Alloy>\n    <TableView id=\"tableview\">\n        <SearchBar id=\"search\" showCancel=\"true\" />\n    </TableView>\n</Alloy>\n```\n"
    }
  ],
